{{!-- Fonts served by the theme itself (no request to a font service): Onest for the interface and
the headings on every page; on posts only, Noto Sans for the text of the article and Google Sans for
its title and its headings; Literata, a choice of the members' display settings (« Police du texte »),
on posts for a member when these settings are on. GENERATED by src/fonts/build-fonts.py from
@fontsource-variable/onest, /noto-sans, /google-sans and /literata (OFL-1.1, assets/fonts/*/OFL.txt):
do not edit by hand. One variable WOFF2 per script subset: the browser only downloads the subsets
whose characters the page uses (unicode-range). Preloaded: Onest latin everywhere, Google Sans latin
and Noto Sans latin on posts from 48rem (the files the first screen needs; on phones the article's
picture fills the first screen and comes first). Literata is never preloaded and keeps the optical
sizes 14 to 28 px only (LITERATA_OPSZ). The fallback faces carry metric overrides so the text barely
moves when the font arrives (font-display: swap). Ghost's custom fonts (Design > Brand > Typography)
still win through --gh-font-heading / --gh-font-body (src/css/base/tokens.css). --}}
<link rel="preload" href="{{asset "fonts/onest/onest-latin.woff2"}}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{{#is "post"}}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{asset "fonts/google-sans/google-sans-latin.woff2"}}" as="font" type="font/woff2" media="(min-width: 48rem)" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" href="{{asset "fonts/noto-sans/noto-sans-latin.woff2"}}" as="font" type="font/woff2" media="(min-width: 48rem)" crossorigin>
{{/is}}
